      Reads CSR_CYCLE/CSR_INSTRET directly via riscv_pmu_ctr_read_csr() with no validation of mcounteren state. If M-mode firmware left mcounteren.CY=0 or mcounteren.IR=0, the RISC-V spec mandates an illegal-instruction trap — but on hardware that instead returns constant/zero values silently, the kernel receives bogus counter data indistinguishable from legitimate reads. No error return path exists; idx outside the two recognised constants returns 0, which is itself silently confused with 'counter value is zero'.
  [RISK] drivers/perf/riscv_pmu.c:134-143  riscv_pmu_ctr_read_csr
