      Consumes raw counter values from the ctr_read callback and commits the delta into event->count. No validation that the counter value represents real hardware activity: a misconfigured counter returning constant/zero produces delta=0 which is indistinguishable from a period with genuinely no events. Once local64_add() commits to event->count, the bogus data propagates to every userspace consumer via read(), mmap, and PERF_EVENT_IOC_PERIOD. The cmpxchg loop (line 173-178) ensures atomicity but not correctness of the underlying data.
